From: Robert-Wang-08 <wang.robert.08@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:26:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(windows): find a PATH command by its PATHEXT
 extension
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`executable()` looked for exactly the configured name in each PATH
directory, so `cli: 'gh'` on Windows never resolved to the `gh.exe` (or
`gh.cmd`) beside it and setup reported the CLI as missing. Windows now
tries the configured name and each PATHEXT extension.

The setup tests ran only on POSIX because their stand-in CLIs were
`#!/bin/sh` scripts. They are now JavaScript run by this node, with a
`.cmd` companion on Windows, so the whole setup path — CLI resolution,
account and repository checks, the Feishu bot checks — is covered on both
platforms instead of skipped.

The packed `*.tgz` at the repository root is a build artifact and is now
ignored.
---
 .gitignore               |  1 +
 src/deployment.ts        |  5 ++-
 tests/deployment.spec.ts | 71 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 3 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

